WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.366
Module thirteen:

2
00:00:01.366 --> 00:00:06.320
the future of decentralized finance and the economy of artificial intelligence

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:06.764
agents.

4
00:00:06.764 --> 00:00:11.591
How an agent gets a wallet, which rules limit it, how agents pay each other,

5
00:00:11.591 --> 00:00:13.814
and who answers for their mistakes.

6
00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:19.737
An agent is a program based on a language model that not only answers but acts.

7
00:00:19.737 --> 00:00:22.167
Nobody will open a bank account for it,

8
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:25.782
and a card payment costs more than a request to a service.

9
00:00:25.782 --> 00:00:29.396
So the agent gets a crypto wallet and pays in stablecoins:

10
00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:32.886
a transfer on a second layer costs a fraction of a cent.

11
00:00:33.886 --> 00:00:36.130
The most dangerous link is the key.

12
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.978
So the agent's wallet is a smart account with its own rules:

13
00:00:39.978 --> 00:00:44.788
it checks who signed, how much, to whom, and whether the limit is exceeded.

14
00:00:44.788 --> 00:00:47.866
The agent gets a session key with narrow rights:

15
00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:51.842
for one day, no more than ten dollars, only to three services.

16
00:00:51.842 --> 00:00:54.022
The main key stays with the human.

17
00:00:55.022 --> 00:00:56.773
A month of an agent's work:

18
00:00:56.773 --> 00:00:59.627
20 requests a day, ten to thirty cents each,

19
00:00:59.627 --> 00:01:03.129
and sometimes it is slipped a fake 200-dollar invoice.

20
00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.723
Without rules, such invoices go through.

21
00:01:05.723 --> 00:01:08.058
Limits and a whitelist cap the loss,

22
00:01:08.058 --> 00:01:11.366
but too low a limit gets in the way of honest work.

23
00:01:12.366 --> 00:01:17.262
An agent needs a payment that is instant, cheap and needs no registration.

24
00:01:17.262 --> 00:01:21.496
The x402 protocol uses the old response code “payment required”:

25
00:01:21.496 --> 00:01:26.855
the service names a price, the agent repeats the request with a signed stablecoin

26
00:01:26.855 --> 00:01:29.634
payment, and the service returns the data.

27
00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:30.494
Alongside it:

28
00:01:30.494 --> 00:01:34.662
mandates signed by a human, and registries of agent reputation.

29
00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.483
An intent is when you sign only what you need:

30
00:01:38.483 --> 00:01:41.121
sell ether no cheaper than a certain price.

31
00:01:41.121 --> 00:01:43.267
How to do it is decided by solvers.

32
00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.230
They compete in a Dutch auction,

33
00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:48.481
where the price gradually worsens down to your bound.

34
00:01:48.481 --> 00:01:50.750
The strongest has no reason to hurry:

35
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.430
it takes the trade just when the second is about to step in.

36
00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:57.585
So the price is set by competition:

37
00:01:57.585 --> 00:02:02.632
the more solvers and the lower their costs, the closer the price is to the market.

38
00:02:02.632 --> 00:02:05.772
Without rivals, the trade goes at your lower bound.

39
00:02:05.772 --> 00:02:09.403
Set it thoughtfully, and do not give an intent a long life:

40
00:02:09.403 --> 00:02:11.558
it is a free option for the solver.

41
00:02:12.558 --> 00:02:17.326
An agent joins a model, which can make mistakes or fall for a hidden command,

42
00:02:17.326 --> 00:02:20.732
with a blockchain, where a transfer cannot be reversed.

43
00:02:20.732 --> 00:02:22.900
An agent has no rights or property,

44
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.368
and almost everywhere its owner answers for its actions.

45
00:02:26.368 --> 00:02:27.359
Hence the rules:

46
00:02:27.359 --> 00:02:32.499
a separate wallet with a budget you can afford to lose, limits at the wallet level,

47
00:02:32.499 --> 00:02:36.462
a human signature for large amounts, and a log of every payment.

48
00:02:37.462 --> 00:02:38.466
The main points.

49
00:02:38.466 --> 00:02:41.228
An agent can be given a wallet and a budget,

50
00:02:41.228 --> 00:02:43.802
and it pays for data and services itself.

51
00:02:43.802 --> 00:02:48.384
Security rests not on the agent's intelligence but on the wallet's rules.

52
00:02:48.384 --> 00:02:52.150
And whoever gave the agent its key answers for its mistakes.
